@ Index:   Tide 47 data: MIDDLE EAST: TICON-3 (8 ports)
@ Author:  Victor Valdes
@ Version: 0.1.0
@ Source:  https://github.com/valdesvj/tide47
@ Tested:  with TIDE47 in the C47 simulator (tests/test_tide47.py)
@ Input:   X = a port's number (1-8), or 0 for the region (called by TIDE47)
@ Output:  the port's name, time zone, datum, source, Z0 and the matrix HG of its harmonic constants
@
@ ---- What it is ----
@ TIDEME is a data program of Tide 47: the harmonic constants of the 8 ports of the region MIDDLE EAST: TICON-3,
@ for TIDE47 to predict their tides. The ports: Mina Salman, Bahrain; Mina Qaboos, Muscat; Masirah, Oman; Salalah,
@ Oman; Chabahar, Iran; Karachi, Pakistan; Aden, Yemen; Djibouti.
@
@ ---- How to use it ----
@ Load it with TIDE47 and press XEQ TIDE47 (not XEQ TIDEME: TIDE47 calls it). Load only the regions you want:
@ TIDE47 finds the data programs on the calculator, and + goes from one region to the next. Load the TIDEME built
@ together with your TIDE47: an older one is left out with OLD DATA, REBUILD.
@
@ ---- What it changes on your calculator ----
@ Called by TIDE47 with a port's number, it sets the port's name, time zone, datum, source and mean level in
@ TIDE47's registers and writes the matrix HG (one number a constituent); TIDE47 deletes HG at its end. Nothing
@ else.
@
@ ---- Programs and labels ----
@ One program with one global label (TIDEME); each port is a local label (LBL 01-8), LBL 99 the region.
@

LBL "TIDEME"                    ; X = 0: the region (GTO 99); else the port X (XEQ IND)
X=0?
GTO 99
STO 99
XEQ IND 99
RTN
LBL 99                          ; the region: its title (R97), its number of ports (R96), the constituents (R93)
"MIDDLE EAST: TICON-3"
STO 97
8
STO 96
60
STO 93
RTN
